  "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer periodic dielectric stack for dichroic filtering. Stack structure: Air incident side, then alternating HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) layers starting with HfO2, ending with SiO2 (Lemarchand) before fused silica substrate. Total 24 layers (12 HfO2 + 12 SiO2 (Lemarchand)). Optimize individual thickness of each layer. Starting point: quarter-wave optical thickness at 550 nm center wavelength (HfO2 ~69 nm, SiO2 (Lemarchand) ~95 nm based on recalled indices n_HfO2≈2.0, n_SiO2 (Lemarchand)≈1.45). Wavelength bands: maximize reflectance in 400-700 nm, maximize transmittance in 1530-1565 nm. Incidence angle: 0 degrees (normal). Polarization: unpolarized (average of TE and TM). Manufacturing constraint: exactly 24 layers, within 30-layer maximum. Materials: hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from catalog. Substrate: fused silica (SiO2 (Lemarchand)).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 24-layer periodic dielectric stack consisting of alternating HfO2 and SiO2 layers (starting with HfO2, ending with SiO2) on a fused-silica substrate at 0° normal incidence under unpolarized illumination. Optimize the physical thickness of each of the 24 coating layers independently, initializing from quarter-wave values at 550 nm. Maximize average reflectance over 400–700 nm and maximize average transmittance over 1530–1565 nm.",
